From: Camera investigation <camera-investigation@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH candidate] media: qcom: camss: Do not enable unconfigured CSID 680 drop and crop

The RDI path enables horizontal and vertical drop and crop without
programming their patterns or windows. Leave those functions disabled
when forwarding the complete frame, as the gen2 path does.

A separate X1E80100 experiment reports frame drops with the current
settings. Test on the affected hardware and collect active clocks and
IRQ evidence before integrating this candidate. The reset cause is not
established.

Link: https://github.com/karsies-wq/sp11-imx681-linux/tree/b08f76f40b8d7b715bd4da6aef484f86142cc147

---
--- a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss-csid-680.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss-csid-680.c
@@ -271,10 +271,6 @@
 	val = RDI_CFG1_TIMESTAMP_STB_FRAME;
 	val |= RDI_CFG1_BYTE_CNTR_EN;
 	val |= RDI_CFG1_TIMESTAMP_EN;
-	val |= RDI_CFG1_DROP_H_EN;
-	val |= RDI_CFG1_DROP_V_EN;
-	val |= RDI_CFG1_CROP_H_EN;
-	val |= RDI_CFG1_CROP_V_EN;
 	val |= RDI_CFG1_PACKING_MIPI;
 
 	writel(val, csid->base + CSID_RDI_CFG1(port));
